# Session recency

Live tmux sessions should be ordered by tmux's `session_last_attached` value.
The picker should initially select the second-most-recent live session so
pressing Enter can switch back to the previous session.

    :bins jj cat sh sleep tmux

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'cat', 'sh', 'sleep', and 'tmux' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s beta "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s gamma "cat" (success)

Build deterministic attachment history. `alpha` remains detached, while the
other sessions are attached in ascending recency order. Sleep between switches
because tmux reports attachment times with one-second resolution.

    :$ sleep 1 (exit: 0)
    :t switch-client -t beta (success)
    :$ sleep 1 (exit: 0)
    :t switch-client -t gamma (success)
    :$ sleep 1 (exit: 0)
    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0

The non-interactive list should put attached sessions in descending recency
order and leave the never-attached `alpha` session last.

    :$ sesh --filter (exit: 0)

```stdout
runner
gamma
beta
alpha
```

Launch the picker in the runner pane with enough height to show the complete
order. The second row, `gamma`, should be selected initially.

    :t resize-window -t runner:0 -x 80 -y 20 (success)
    :$ tmux respawn-pane -k 'sesh; : > picker-exited; cat' (exit: 0)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :snap

```terminal
session:
  4/4 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
                                                                               ┃
 ⬤ runner                                                                      ┃
▌⬤ gamma                                                                       ┃
 ⬤ beta                                                                        ┃
 ⬤ alpha                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────












```

Accept the initial selection after tmux's timestamp advances, then synchronize
on both the client switch and picker exit.

    :$ sleep 1 (exit: 0)
    :t set-hook -g client-session-changed "set-hook -gu client-session-changed; wait-for -S recency-switched" (success)
    :k enter
    :t wait-for recency-switched (success)
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f picker-exited; do :; done' (exit: 0)

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
gamma
```

Tmux should update `gamma`'s attachment time itself, making it the most recent
session without `sesh` writing any metadata.

    :$ sesh --filter (exit: 0)

```stdout
gamma
runner
beta
alpha
```

